393},"altText":"Grilled Chicken Roasted Sweet Potato Caesar Salad"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bt8b0","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c4pn0","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Since we live in the Northwest where I knew I could get some great Dungeness I decided it was time to give this a try when we got home. So this is how it went.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6qt64","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"e3nts","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"aodus","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"First I bought a whole cooked dungeness crab, next time I will buy two! This is so good!","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"1sdcg","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_83487100ab4d4a2d95ad2d9bafcf3a55~mv2_d_3943_2638_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":3943,"height":2638},"altText":"Szechuan Salt & Pepper Dungeness Crab with Shrimp"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7c81b","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I took off the back of the crab and removed all the gills, crab butter etc and rinsed well. Then I decided to add one pound of large shrimp that were raw with the shells on, heads off and deveined.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"2g9dn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"40ffc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Next I added about 1/3 cup of potato starch to a large Ziploc bag and tossed the shrimp inside to coat them well. Leaving the shells on helps the shrimp to retain moisture through the cooking process and helps keep the finger licking seasonings on the shrimp.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ct1md","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7lj8h","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fe1du","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6nrre","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Now it was time for the fryer! My fryer was heated to 375 degrees and the shrimp took about 2 or 3 minutes. I turned them out onto a ceramic serving dish while I fried the Dungeness in the same way as I heated up the wok and added the spices.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dntr4","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"oq1","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_76357d084abc4bc6bb95fab5ea938d53~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Szechuan Salt & Pepper Dungeness Crab with Shrimp"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ec59c","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" If you don't have a deep fryer you can use a large dutch oven or deep skillet by adding about 3 cups of oil. Bring it to temp if you have a thermometer or test by adding a cube of bread to see if it fry's up nicely. Use a large slotted spoon to scoop the shrimp and crab parts out of the oil and onto your serving dish.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"a5d20","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"20upn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Here you can see I started roasting some asparagus in a cast iron skillet for a side dish. I snapped the ends to get rid of any woodiness then rinsed and put them into a very lightly oiled skillet on medium heat. I just roll them around a few times while they begin to brown slightly and soften until they are done to the texture I like. I don't add any salt or seasonings most of the time but I do like to use a little bit of a nice finishing salt at the table. I have some smoked Himalayan salt that I smoked last fall that I'm using right now. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"etn2e","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"2okkp","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_685aa8641e1c40a4b3b59ef967a35a8c~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Szechuan Salt & Pepper Dungeness Crab with Shrimp"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4drv2","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"a54fo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Now it was time for the wok. You could use a deep skillet for this as well. I added 3 tablespoons of grape seed oil and started heating up my wok just before I put the shrimp in the fryer. I added the salt & pepper seasoning mix and one minced Serrano chili pepper. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7t6nm","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"38hg2","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"builn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"77oe0","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_02ab7ccb86af4de78c68e6f6b657c329~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":""}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9he6s","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"e805d","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"When the oil was shimmering on the surface I added the deep fried crab directly from the fryer and tossed in some chopped  scallions. Stirring quickly with my slotted spoon I coated the crab with the spices thoroughly.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7sohb","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"fiei","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_421ff09c367e470dba7b589f6c00c4ab~mv2_d_4032_2685_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":2685},"altText":"Szechuan Salt & Pepper Dungeness Crab with Shrimp"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5m5gp","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"95vmj","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Then I added the shrimp to the wok with the crab and tossed it around a bit more before pouring the whole wok back into the serving dish along with as much of the tasty seasoned oil as possible.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8vi8q","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"klkc","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_b08b77de2a624219a34a6dc12950cf17~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Szechuan Salt & Pepper Dungeness Crab with Shrimp"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"190r1","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" And there you have it, break out the napkins and crab cracking equipment! It's time to get busy!","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlig